From rpy-list at maubp.freeserve.co.uk  Wed Dec 17 10:22:51 2008
From: rpy-list at maubp.freeserve.co.uk (Peter)
Date: Wed, 17 Dec 2008 10:22:51 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rpy] Problem with R's hist() function
In-Reply-To: <d9bfa52b0812161700t338a13d5v97c88bc0c24cf33b@mail.gmail.com>
References: <d9bfa52b0812161700t338a13d5v97c88bc0c24cf33b@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <320fb6e00812170222q1a6da152vb9c5be4a9328d363@mail.gmail.com>

On Wed, Dec 17, 2008 at 1:00 AM, Marcos Silva <marcosfs2006 at gmail.com> wrote:
> Hello People, it's me again...
>
> I  tried to use the R's hist() function, using this code:
>
> hist = robjects.r['hist']
> x = robjects.FloatVector(dataset)
> hist(x)
> ...
> But the graphic that I got was very strange...
> I cannot figure out what is wrong...

By default, R uses the dataset's column names (or something like that)
which with rpy(2) have probably defaulted to some long string of their
actual data.  You'll see lots of strange text (mostly numbers) all
over your graphs as a result.  You will need to explicitly set the
graph captions, and then everything is fine.

Peter

